%n [...] u mahīram sanqam
#note: The reading of the sign sequence @akk{ZA.AN.GA} follows @bib{temp_id_4487036324091982@86}. The adjectiv seems to be derived from the scarcely-attested verb @i{sanāqu} B “to be in need of”, which @bib{RN2721@S, 145b}, with reference to @bib{RN1644@265} lists as an Aramaic loanword. Note, however, that von Soden (@i{ibid}.) understands the related noun @i{sunqu} “famine” as proper Akkadian. For a discussion of the sign sequence @akk{ZA.AN.GA} with its parallel in the MB version of the Cuthaean Legend, see @bib{RN262@278f.}.
// cf. L I.12 MB "A" b+11
